## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design per-tenant privacy controls in a real-world multi-tenant GCP SaaS, balancing performance, data isolation, and compliance.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time data redaction with Cloud DLP integrated into Dataflow pipelines
- Per-tenant Cloud Storage buckets and BigQuery datasets with CMEK-managed encryption
- IAM Conditions for tenant-scoped least-privilege access controls
- Synthetic-tenant CI validation with automated rollback on policy violations

## Code Example
```terraform
# Per-tenant IAM condition binding
resource "google_project_iam_binding" "tenant_access" {
  project = var.project_id
  role    = "roles/storage.objectViewer"
  members = ["serviceAccount:${var.analyst_sa}"]
  condition {
    title       = "tenant_isolation_${var.tenant_id}"
    description = "Restrict access to tenant ${var.tenant_id} data only"
    expression  = "resource.labels.tenant_id == '${var.tenant_id}'"
  }
}

# Per-tenant Cloud Storage bucket with CMEK
resource "google_storage_bucket" "tenant_bucket" {
  name     = "${var.project_id}-data-${var.tenant_id}"
  location = var.region
  encryption {
    default_kms_key_name = google_kms_crypto_key.tenant_key.id
  }
  labels = {
    tenant_id = var.tenant_id
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates the ability to design tenant-isolated logging architecture using Cloud Logging sinks, IAM least privilege principles, CMEK encryption, and automated validation in a shared GCP project multi-tenant environment.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant log sinks with resource and label-based filtering
- Least-privilege IAM roles for secure log export operations
- Customer-managed encryption keys (CMEK) for log data protection
- Log-based monitoring and alerting for leakage detection
- CI/CD automated validation using synthetic tenant provisioning

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: validate tenant log isolation in CI pipeline
const tenantId = process.env.TENANT_ID;
const logs = readLogs({
  filter: `resource.labels.tenant_id="${tenantId}"`,
  timeRange: '1h'
});

// Verify no cross-tenant log contamination
const crossTenantLeaks = logs.filter(log => 
  log.labels.tenant_id !== tenantId
);

if (crossTenantLeaks.length > 0) {
  throw new Error('Tenant log isolation violation detected');
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests on-demand, auditable access in a shared GCP workspace, ensuring least privilege and robust revocation.

## Key Concepts

- IAM Conditions

- Access Context Manager

- VPC Service Controls

- Auditability and synthetic validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example policy binding (pseudo)
{
  \"bindings\": [
    {
      \"role\": \"roles/bigquery.dataViewer\",
      \"members\": [\"serviceAccount:auditor@example.iam.gserviceaccount.com\"],
      \"condition\": {
        \"title\": \"tenantScope\",
        \"expression\": \"resource.name.startsWith('projects/tenant-123/datasets/tenant_123_') && request.time < timestamp('2026-12-01T00:00:00Z')\"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

